{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work","id":1004586,"title":"How would a WoD computer/video game would work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-17T12:54:33-08:00","id":1004586,"title":"How would a WoD computer/video game would work?","content":"If there's a new WoD game particularly or especially Vampire how can it work out?<br /> <br /> Well I was thinking of somehow making a Vampire game that somehow doesn't fall into the same &quot;Camarilla game seven clans only&quot; pitfall that Bloodlines used since I would actually like to see a game where all 13 clans are available to play as (since I'm actually dying to play as a Caitiff, Lasombra and Tzimisce clans) and of course it could be a &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; with a Vampire central focus?<br /> <br /> For example, what about starting the game as a shovelhead but maybe instead you were dugged out by a another vampire who recovers you which I would rather have the Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs be treated as either joinable or opposable factions which works like Fallout New Vegas?<br /> <br /> Or maybe &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; is actually where all supernatural splats are playable?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T13:15:29-08:00","id":1004592,"title":"","content":"I don't know too much about Vampire, but I've thought about how a Werewolf game would look. My hope would be for them to do it old school like Neverwinter Nights. Create your pack, picking their auspice, their stats/gifts ect and go into the game that way. I think that would be the best way to keep the feel of Werewolf being pack centered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T16:09:22-08:00","id":1004690,"title":"","content":"I can see an MMO WoD game that let's you play as any splat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T20:53:56-08:00","id":1004789,"title":"","content":"Well, Bloodlines for Vampire is (or just was?) on sale on Good old Games.<br /> <br /> The planned MMO died.<br /> <br /> I actually got to see some of the dead Werewolf game at Gen Con in Milwaukee, but the company died and left the rights in limbo despite it being nearly done.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T04:07:21-08:00","id":1004868,"title":"","content":"Well, as a developer with some past in the video game industry, I thinkt it would be hard to have a good video game for WoD.<br /> When I played bloodlines (very recently), what shocked me the most was the simplification/rework of disciplines.<br /> Presence was a debuff around you, Auspex was a buff on your character and most disciplines were reworked to have the same functionality as celerity/potence/fortitude, you had an effect for each disciplines and each level increased this effect.<br /> <br /> At first, I was somehow sad/disappointed, but as I played, I understood that those simplification were a necessity. Disciplines, like Obtenebration/Necromancy/Thaumaturgy, are far too complex to be implemented in a video game.<br /> You have far too many different effect with even more in-game application.<br /> Domination alone have so many application it's very hard to implement in a game. And it's a discipline that I consider &quot;simple&quot;.<br /> In fact, when you have a very complex disciplines, it may seems like nothing but it's a lot of work (and I really mean it) just to make it simpler and playable.<br /> You need to keep the essence of the original discipline while removing most complexities/effect.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s take the example of Auspex in bloodlines. This discipline allowed the player to see NPC's aura and boosted your Wits/Perception.<br /> The boost to Wits/Perception was a buff to your character that simulated Heightened Senses while improving your firearm ability in combat.<br /> But, being able to see NPC's aura was useless, completely. There was no NPC hiding his nature or something similar that would give Aura Perception some usefulness.<br /> So, instead, they've added an effect to the discipline, you can see aura through walls and each level of Auspex improve your vision's distance.<br /> When you look at it, this difference was weird, Auspex never allowed you to see aura's through walls so why did they add this?<br /> Because it allowed you to see that someone was in a room, which was similar to hearing someone movement/heartbeat in the tabletop version.<br /> It also added usefulness to Auspex during infiltration by allowing you to see NPCs patrolling.<br /> <br /> This simplification of disciplines was necessary, but with it, the game became (in my opinion) somehow tasteless.<br /> Disciplines were a little too similar to one another and the roleplaying part was kind of lost. Having a Brujah, a Toreador or a Ventrue would have little to no difference.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I loved the first NPC Malkavian you met in the game, the quest around her and her clan weakness was awesome.<br /> More generally, the world, the atmosphere you had in it, the NPC's, it was great, very immersive, very dark. Just how I pictures World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> So having a video-game regrouping World of Darkness would be a tremendous amount of work just to rework (most) abilities for every &quot;race&quot;.<br /> I would really love to see one but for this to happen, a very serious rework of discipline is required.<br /> <br /> I think that the easiest way would be to have more an adventure game instead of an RPG.<br /> By losing some part of the character customization, specifically the clan choice, you would be in total control of what powers the player have and you would be able to design those powers more deeply.<br /> Even if I love the character customization part, I think that WoD is more about horror and story than your clan or some skill, and, focusing on it would be better than loosing resources to adapt a tabletop system into a video-game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, please forgive my mistakes","edited":{"userid":12400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12400-garyo","user":"GaryO","date":". 11-18-2016, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12400-garyo","name":"GaryO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12400_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T20:04:19-08:00","id":1005208,"title":"","content":"Now if you think Disciplines from Vampire were simplified, imagine what would need to happen to <i>Mage's Spheres</i>. Even if we assume loads of functions would be flat-out ignored because they aren't strictly necessary (Wonder/Fetish crafting, Dream walking, time travel, layering different locations on top of each other, etc), the Spheres capabilities would need to be curtailed because some abilities are too difficult to program for as open-ended as they are.<br /> <br /> That said, this isn't quite as difficult as one might imagine, for one very good reason: Mage Paradigms. Simply make every playable Mage character believe in limitations to their Spheres (or simply not have access to knowledge that would let them push the boundaries) that work within the game's mechanical limitations. Time 2 doesn't give you open-ended understanding of the past or future, but it could be used to give the player flashbacks at certain locations, or for combat increasing their dodging ability (they can see the attacks coming). Forces 5 won't summon a hurricane, but it can bring lightning down on an enemy's head. Etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T00:55:19-08:00","id":1005273,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines came out in 2003 or 2004 didn't it? Games are enormously more complex these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T04:42:50-08:00","id":1006119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work#post1004586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, what about starting the game as a shovelhead but maybe instead you were dugged out by a another vampire who recovers you which I would rather have the Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs be treated as either joinable or opposable factions which works like Fallout New Vegas?</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I like New Vegas, the faction system was so messy and bugged that my head hurts every time I bother with it. It's a great concept, but too difficult to produce.<br /> A more linear game might sound less ambitious, but the less complicated the game, the easier it gets for developers to focus on quality.<br /> <br /> Now for shovelheads, people really missed the point on those. Shovelheads weren't meant to be the standard PC, they're not meant to be even played as vampires, shovelheads are at the same level as ghouls.<br /> <br /> Just like Camarilla use ghouls, Fallen use thralls, Kuei-Jin use bakemono and Dhampir...the Sabbat uses Shovelheads, mancurians, Szlachta and ghouls.<br /> <br /> The shovelhead is a valid character concept, but very limited. Other than not having the privilege of recognized sect membership, they're expendable, they are limited to frenzying/feeding/killing and cleaning duty and rarely survive more than a few nights (if they even survived the embrace). Tzimisce themselves claim that hardly 1 over a thousand shovelheads are worth keeping, and those few aren't considered shovelheads anymore.<br /> <br /> It's true that WoD video games are typically action oriented, but at least for VtM, there is room for more interesting gameplay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well I was thinking of somehow making a Vampire game that somehow doesn't fall into the same &quot;Camarilla game seven clans only&quot; pitfall that Bloodlines used since I would actually like to see a game where all 13 clans are available to play as (since I'm actually dying to play as a Caitiff, Lasombra and Tzimisce clans) and of course it could be a &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; with a Vampire central focus? </div> </div> </div>In one single video-game? that would be impossible.<br /> <br /> The seven Clan in Bloodlines isn't a 'pitfall', it's actually a stretch, and the developers didn't even finish the game. It was such a mess that the clans were hardly relevant in the plot.<br /> <br /> And now you want to make things worse?...no, it's better if the devs focus on a few characters (two or three max) and develop an interesting, well-fleshed story behind them, with the relevant gameplay.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T16:15:44-08:00","id":1006455,"title":"","content":"I do see a werewolf the apocalypse (or even a hypothetical CofD werewolf the forsaken, since they included it in the survey) video game as being similar to a GTA V/Payday 2/RPG hybrid. You plan out your raids on the wyrmish targets in intricate detail for the biggest quests, in a manner similar to the preplanning in Payday 2, decide what if any kinfolk (or wolf blooded) help to bring like in GTA V and the smaller quests are planned the same way as the smaller heists in payday 2 with simple assets you can hire or have planted. I feel that approach really nails the pack tactics element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T00:15:21-08:00","id":1006614,"title":"","content":"The problem with a WoD v\u00eddeo game is that the WoD is barely a game, if at all. It's mostly just a jumble of systematically for doing stuff. All you're supposed to do in game is do what your character would do and arbitrarily get retarded experience. There's very little in the way of an assumed goal or story structure. Dungeons &amp; Dragons and lends itselfhave itself to an existing genre of video game. You go on adventures, kill monsters, earn specific amountsto of treasure, level up, repeat. Starting with the World of Darkness as your idea for a v\u00eddeo game doesn't get you much of anywhere in terms of game design. And when you finish designing your World of Darkness video game, it won't really feel like the WoD, because the WoD isn't really a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T00:24:01-08:00","id":1006616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Sluagh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1006614#post1006614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with a WoD v\u00eddeo game is that the WoD is barely a game, if at all. It's mostly just a jumble of systematically for doing stuff. All you're supposed to do in game is do what your character would do and arbitrarily get retarded experience. There's very little in the way of an assumed goal or story structure. Dungeons &amp; Dragons and lends itselfhave itself to an existing genre of video game. You go on adventures, kill monsters, earn specific amountsto of treasure, level up, repeat. Starting with the World of Darkness as your idea for a v\u00eddeo game doesn't get you much of anywhere in terms of game design. And when you finish designing your World of Darkness video game, it won't really feel like the WoD, because the WoD isn't really a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda disagree since a ideal WoD video/computer game or rather it's main campaign can work cross between Deus Ex and Fallout NV which consists of the &quot;Main Questline&quot; along with side quests while exploring several cities and such.<br /> <br /> Also the closest to actual &quot;storytelling game&quot; it can get is actually releasing the game's source code, modding tools, level editor, etc and creating your own campaigns which the mod maker is sorta of a storyteller in a way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T03:08:33-08:00","id":1007123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1005208#post1005208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now if you think Disciplines from Vampire were simplified, imagine what would need to happen to <i>Mage's Spheres</i>. Even if we assume loads of functions would be flat-out ignored because they aren't strictly necessary (Wonder/Fetish crafting, Dream walking, time travel, layering different locations on top of each other, etc), the Spheres capabilities would need to be curtailed because some abilities are too difficult to program for as open-ended as they are.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You could be playing a Technocrat. An Enforcer taking down the SPD as an FPS, a Void Engineer (or a whole Amalgam) going on missions like Mass Effect, an NWO for a Hitman-esque game. You could also add alternative endings/morality: the Void Engineer could choose not to Format Space or Sanitize Nodes (culminating in becoming a Dreamspeaker at the end, which gives access to dynamic Magick in the final level) and the Enforcer could redeem an aspect of the Wyrm in a secret 101 % completion ending. In between missions there would be mini-games for research and development, that would influence the plot and mission structure.<br /> For everyone there would of course be an option of joining the Nephandi. (And The Harlot Empress, The Aswad of Prime, or Jodi Blake could be on all the boxes.)<br /> <br /> Each Convention and each Methodology could get their own game, for a start. The game for the Ivory Tower could be a top-down management game, perhaps? This has the benefits of presenting the whole World of Darkness (the Progenitor game could be a cross-over with VtM etc.) and introducing Mage without having to design &amp; program a full True Magick system. And of course it promotes the Technocracy's perspective and ideals!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-31-2017, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T07:13:30-08:00","id":1007221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1004868#post1004868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as a developer with some past in the video game industry, I thinkt it would be hard to have a good video game for WoD.<br /> When I played bloodlines (very recently), what shocked me the most was the simplification/rework of disciplines.<br /> Presence was a debuff around you, Auspex was a buff on your character and most disciplines were reworked to have the same functionality as celerity/potence/fortitude, you had an effect for each disciplines and each level increased this effect.<br /> <br /> At first, I was somehow sad/disappointed, but as I played, I understood that those simplification were a necessity. Disciplines, like Obtenebration/Necromancy/Thaumaturgy, are far too complex to be implemented in a video game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I's sure you could make even those disciplines work, you have to change them a bit, but you definitely could.<br /> <br /> Take Obtenebration for example:<br /> <br /> 1dot: Shadow Play = player causes a darkening effect within a certin radius around themselves and NPC visibility is decreased, making it easier to sneak.<br /> <br /> 2dot: Shroud of Night = player targets an NPC who is then consumed by a mass of blackness, the NPC flails about in panic and begins moving around the area aimlessly until the mass dissipates.<br /> <br /> 3dot: Arms of the Abyss = player looks at a surface and spawns a shadowy tentacle there, which can then grab nearby enemies and hold them in place.<br /> <br /> 4dot: Black Metamorphosis = just as in the TT the player transforms into a shadow creature, his regular melee attacks are replaced with a long black shadow whip, like Dracula from that Castlevania reboot.<br /> <br /> 5dot: Tenebrous Form = Again, same as TT: player turns into a cloud of darkness and is imune to damage, able to pass through NPCs, and when it comes to closed or locked doors triggers an animation where it flows through the gaps.<br /> <br /> I could probably come up with a way to simulate the other disciplines, if there are other disciplines I could explain how to simulate those too if anyone would like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1006616#post1006616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kinda disagree since a ideal WoD video/computer game or rather it's main campaign can work cross between Deus Ex and Fallout NV which consists of the &quot;Main Questline&quot; along with side quests while exploring several cities and such.<br /> <br /> Also the closest to actual &quot;storytelling game&quot; it can get is actually releasing the game's source code, modding tools, level editor, etc and creating your own campaigns which the mod maker is sorta of a storyteller in a way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much exactly what I would like to see, especially what you said about modding tools, full mod support like you see in Bethesda's RPG titles is the closest a video game can come TT storyteller experience.<br /> <br /> Let's hope Paradox+Obsidian are reading. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T12:58:11-08:00","id":1007388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007123#post1007123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could be playing a Technocrat. An Enforcer taking down the SPD as an FPS, a Void Engineer (or a whole Amalgam) going on missions like Mass Effect, an NWO for a Hitman-esque game. You could also add alternative endings/morality: the Void Engineer could choose not to Format Space or Sanitize Nodes (culminating in becoming a Dreamspeaker at the end, which gives access to dynamic Magick in the final level) and the Enforcer could redeem an aspect of the Wyrm in a secret 101 % completion ending. In between missions there would be mini-games for research and development, that would influence the plot and mission structure.<br /> For everyone there would of course be an option of joining the Nephandi. (And The Harlot Empress or Jodi Blake could be on all the boxes.)<br /> <br /> Each Convention and each Methodology could get their own game, for a start. The game for the Ivory Tower could be a top-down management game, perhaps? This has the benefits of presenting the whole World of Darkness (the Progenitor game could be a cross-over with VtM etc.) and introducing Mage without having to design &amp; program a full True Magick system. And of course it promotes the Technocracy's perspective and ideals!</div> </div> </div> </div>You could have the Progenitor game revolve around an agent of Damage Control going out and, well, controlling some damage. Clearing out a rogue Progenitor's laboratory of unsanctioned bio-experiments. Containing an outbreak of disease that mutates its victims. Breaking into a Etherite's compound and putting down their Frankenstein creations (I recommend reading a manga called Embalming, for inspiration on creative Frankenstein monsters). Sanitizing a Tzimisce's haven (like your VtM idea above), which could be further complicated by subordinate Sabbat packs and even the Tzimisce's Koldunic sorcery.<br /> <br /> And all throughout, a slowly building plot related to this weird thing called &quot;Pentex&quot;. Culminating in a raid on an SPD research lab, overrun by Fomori and brainwashed Technocrats. You can even have a Nephandus as the final boss, sitting on top of a tower, trying to perform a ritual to summon a powerful Wyrm manifestation.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, I want to play that game. Damage Control is awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T08:32:00-08:00","id":1007713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007221#post1007221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I's sure you could make even those disciplines work, you have to change them a bit, but you definitely could.<br /> <br /> Take Obtenebration for example:<br /> <br /> 1dot: Shadow Play = player causes a darkening effect within a certin radius around themselves and NPC visibility is decreased, making it easier to sneak.<br /> <br /> 2dot: Shroud of Night = player targets an NPC who is then consumed by a mass of blackness, the NPC flails about in panic and begins moving around the area aimlessly until the mass dissipates.<br /> <br /> 3dot: Arms of the Abyss = player looks at a surface and spawns a shadowy tentacle there, which can then grab nearby enemies and hold them in place.<br /> <br /> 4dot: Black Metamorphosis = just as in the TT the player transforms into a shadow creature, his regular melee attacks are replaced with a long black shadow whip, like Dracula from that Castlevania reboot.<br /> <br /> 5dot: Tenebrous Form = Again, same as TT: player turns into a cloud of darkness and is imune to damage, able to pass through NPCs, and when it comes to closed or locked doors triggers an animation where it flows through the gaps.<br /> <br /> I could probably come up with a way to simulate the other disciplines, if there are other disciplines I could explain how to simulate those too if anyone would like.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, I used a shortcut. Of course you can implement on specific discipline into the game, what I wanted to say is that these disciplines require a lot of work both in term of development and gameplay.<br /> If you have the following system: One Disciple Dot - One Spell as you describe above, you'll quickly have too many spell.<br /> You'll have to use a spell bar (like in Dragon Age or World of Warcraft), have something like a spell book and allow the user to bind/unbind his shortcut.<br /> This system, while perfectly viable for PC is hard to use on console because you have less shortcut available.<br /> You could decide to limit the size of the spell bar to 6, so PC and console player have the same number of spell and the portability for a system to another is easier but somehow frustrating because a player will never be able to use all his abilities.<br /> Or you could decide to create a PC-only game, but you're also losing an important part of the market.<br /> <br /> Moreover, when I said that Obtenebration was too complex, this is what I had in mind:<br /> <br /> The second ability, Shroud of Night create a gaseous darkness around the player (or its target if you prefer).<br /> In a game, objects are usually linked to a mesh, a 3D model with triangles.<br /> When you want to add an &quot;effect&quot;, like fire or smoke, you create a particle system.<br /> Particle systems are quite complex so I'll not explain it here, but what you need to keep in mind is that it creates multiple small particles that moves together.<br /> Now, with Shroud of Night you allow the user to create a particle system almost anywhere.<br /> The particles should behave somehow like gas and be &quot;stopped&quot; by a wall for example.<br /> I'm sure you've already seen some buggy game physics with 3D-objects, well with particle it's far worse.<br /> Handling collision with particles is horrible, it put a huge stress on the GPU and can require days of optimization.<br /> And at the end what do you have? Well only the second ability of Obtenebration...<br /> <br /> Additionally, you have to work on a shader for this &quot;gaseous darkness&quot; and shaders are also horribly complex.<br /> For example, the most famous shader for its complexity is the water shader.<br /> One could assume that, nowadays with the huge amount of game released, having a nice and smooth water effect would be pretty easy, but it's not the case.<br /> <a href=\"http://motherboard.vice.com/read/rendering-realistic-water-is-still-game-developments-moby-dick\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>'s an article explaining why and <a href=\"http://blog.bonzaisoftware.com/tnp/gl-water-tutorial/\" target=\"_blank\">here </a>is a tutorial to create a water shader (if you're curious).<br /> Moreover, shaders have a huge impact on the cost of the video game. They require highly skilled and experienced developer and, as you can imagine, they're not cheap.<br /> <br /> So, when creating your video game, you need to ask yourself where do you want to put you money?<br /> Do you develop a very complex discipline like Obtenebration that'll be used only when the player chooses Lasombra as a clan or do you invest money into improving the rest of the game and remove the Lasombra clan from the game?<br /> If you want an example, The Witcher 3 had a development cost estimated at 15 million US dollars, and CD projekt used their own technology for the game engine, reducing the overall cost.<br /> That's already quite a expensive, and you still need to add 25 million for the marketing and distribution of the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, please forgive my mistakes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12400-garyo","name":"GaryO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12400_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:36:56-08:00","id":1007809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007713#post1007713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My bad, I used a shortcut. Of course you can implement on specific discipline into the game, what I wanted to say is that these disciplines require a lot of work both in term of development and gameplay.<br /> If you have the following system: One Disciple Dot - One Spell as you describe above, you'll quickly have too many spell.<br /> You'll have to use a spell bar (like in Dragon Age or World of Warcraft), have something like a spell book and allow the user to bind/unbind his shortcut.<br /> This system, while perfectly viable for PC is hard to use on console because you have less shortcut available.<br /> You could decide to limit the size of the spell bar to 6, so PC and console player have the same number of spell and the portability for a system to another is easier but somehow frustrating because a player will never be able to use all his abilities.<br /> Or you could decide to create a PC-only game, but you're also losing an important part of the market.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit I have never really played a console game, so I'm not sure how this would work; but the way I imagine it you would have each discipline connected to a certain hotkey, and then scroll the mouse wheel to select each &quot;dot&quot;. Again, not sure how or if you could transfer that to console, but it's what I have in mind for a PC experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007713#post1007713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Moreover, when I said that Obtenebration was too complex, this is what I had in mind:<br /> <br /> The second ability, Shroud of Night create a gaseous darkness around the player (or its target if you prefer).<br /> In a game, objects are usually linked to a mesh, a 3D model with triangles.<br /> When you want to add an &quot;effect&quot;, like fire or smoke, you create a particle system.<br /> Particle systems are quite complex so I'll not explain it here, but what you need to keep in mind is that it creates multiple small particles that moves together.<br /> Now, with Shroud of Night you allow the user to create a particle system almost anywhere.<br /> The particles should behave somehow like gas and be &quot;stopped&quot; by a wall for example.<br /> I'm sure you've already seen some buggy game physics with 3D-objects, well with particle it's far worse.<br /> Handling collision with particles is horrible, it put a huge stress on the GPU and can require days of optimization.<br /> And at the end what do you have? Well only the second ability of Obtenebration...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The way I imagine it working would be somewhat like how the &quot;Bat Swarm&quot; in Castlevania: Lords of Shadow 2, go to about 9:00 of this video:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7b7gy5-HgRs?t=9m\" data-code=\"7b7gy5-HgRs\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7b7gy5-HgRs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Notice how the player must first lock-on to the guard and &quot;fires&quot; the bat swarm. Basically any time a player does this the targeted guard is imobilized and the player is able to sneak past. Basically it seems the guard plays an animation, he is unable to see the player, and a particle effect is &quot;connected&quot; to the guard in some way. I'm sure you know more about how that kind of system would be implemented the me though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007713#post1007713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Additionally, you have to work on a shader for this &quot;gaseous darkness&quot; and shaders are also horribly complex.<br /> For example, the most famous shader for its complexity is the water shader.<br /> One could assume that, nowadays with the huge amount of game released, having a nice and smooth water effect would be pretty easy, but it's not the case.<br /> <a href=\"http://motherboard.vice.com/read/rendering-realistic-water-is-still-game-developments-moby-dick\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>'s an article explaining why and <a href=\"http://blog.bonzaisoftware.com/tnp/gl-water-tutorial/\" target=\"_blank\">here </a>is a tutorial to create a water shader (if you're curious).<br /> Moreover, shaders have a huge impact on the cost of the video game. They require highly skilled and experienced developer and, as you can imagine, they're not cheap.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Does that also apply to, say, the spell effects in Skyrim? There are quiet a few of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007713#post1007713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, when creating your video game, you need to ask yourself where do you want to put you money?<br /> Do you develop a very complex discipline like Obtenebration that'll be used only when the player chooses Lasombra as a clan or do you invest money into improving the rest of the game and remove the Lasombra clan from the game?<br /> If you want an example, The Witcher 3 had a development cost estimated at 15 million US dollars, and CD projekt used their own technology for the game engine, reducing the overall cost.<br /> That's already quite a expensive, and you still need to add 25 million for the marketing and distribution of the game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is saying that a WoD game should be low-budget.<br /> <br /> If Paradox doesn't feel they have the resources to do the license proper justice they probably shouldn't have bought the rights.<br /> <br /> Also, in regards to CD projekt using it's own technology, Unreal Engine recently became free, so any potential WoD developer could use that engine instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T13:38:37-08:00","id":1007826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007388#post1007388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have the Progenitor game revolve around an agent of Damage Control going out and, well, controlling some damage. Clearing out a rogue Progenitor's laboratory of unsanctioned bio-experiments. Containing an outbreak of disease that mutates its victims. Breaking into a Etherite's compound and putting down their Frankenstein creations (I recommend reading a manga called Embalming, for inspiration on creative Frankenstein monsters). Sanitizing a Tzimisce's haven (like your VtM idea above), which could be further complicated by subordinate Sabbat packs and even the Tzimisce's Koldunic sorcery.<br /> <br /> And all throughout, a slowly building plot related to this weird thing called &quot;Pentex&quot;. Culminating in a raid on an SPD research lab, overrun by Fomori and brainwashed Technocrats. You can even have a Nephandus as the final boss, sitting on top of a tower, trying to perform a ritual to summon a powerful Wyrm manifestation.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, I want to play that game. Damage Control is awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Damage Control would be a good starting point, with it's focus on covering up sticky situations and making up for mistakes; playing a doctor/biologist would also be novel, I think? Effects and Procedures could be chosen at mission deployment, and in the lab you could customize your 'Hulk-out' form(s).<br /> <br /> Another reason to use Technocracy is because I think it is a very unique concept in fiction - that of some Mages choosing to catalyze their capabilities through science. It's a combination of transhumanity, the shadow conspiracy, and paranormal researchers. An intro of the player character going around a large Construct. The Technocracy's role in covering up the supernatural (for the good of the Masses), controlling the Consensus, pushing the boundaries of science, exploring the universe and keeping Earth safe could all be shown or alluded to.<br /> Characters would talk about using Correspondence: Data to neutralize mystics' scrying, using drug cocktails to block telepathy, and countering divinations with psychological profiling. All of this would make it clear to players that this is not your average conspiracy. I'd say that a well presented Technocracy has potential to be more gripping than mystic Mages (in such an introduction). It could very well be on the par with Half-Life <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hsTEoGoAxUk\" target=\"_blank\">One</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y_3vMUOayyc\" target=\"_blank\">Two</a> and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z3RHenh8vJ8\" target=\"_blank\">Bioshock 1 </a>intros<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007388#post1007388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You can even have a Nephandus as the final boss, sitting on top of a tower, trying to perform a ritual to summon a powerful Wyrm manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>:-)<br /> And that after a whole game of your superiors telling you that <b>everything </b>can be explained through science and intellect. Perhaps Inspired Biochemistry can explain some Fomori, but what explanations it has when confronted with a Greater Bane? (Though I'd guess it has plenty...&quot;An organism for whome acts of emotional significance act as a stimuli to enable feedback-loop processes, which allow it to synthesize compounds to grow in capabilities.&quot;)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007713#post1007713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, when creating your video game, you need to ask yourself where do you want to put you money? Do you develop a very complex discipline like Obtenebration that'll be used only when the player chooses Lasombra as a clan or do you invest money into improving the rest of the game and remove the Lasombra clan from the game?<br /> If you want an example, The Witcher 3 had a development cost estimated at 15 million US dollars, and CD projekt used their own technology for the game engine, reducing the overall cost.<br /> That's already quite a expensive, and you still need to add 25 million for the marketing and distribution of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing a New World Order member could be the budget option. It would be hard to write the plot, dialogues and twists so that it simulates an NWO's mastery of Mind. But from what you said about technology costs, it is certainly cheaper to hire good writers and designers to write for an NWO game; compared to programming in different mystical powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:43:50-08:00","id":1008055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007809#post1007809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to admit I have never really played a console game, so I'm not sure how this would work; but the way I imagine it you would have each discipline connected to a certain hotkey, and then scroll the mouse wheel to select each &quot;dot&quot;. Again, not sure how or if you could transfer that to console, but it's what I have in mind for a PC experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I have but a few years of experience and I'm into programming, not game design so I don't know what is the solution; but the market share of PC is roughly the same as console (ps4 + xbox one), so by limiting to a system you lose around 50% of your potential revenue.<br /> This is a very big deal and most companies require their game designer to think with both pc and console gameplay in mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007809#post1007809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I imagine it working would be somewhat like how the &quot;Bat Swarm&quot; in Castlevania: Lords of Shadow 2, go to about 9:00 of this video:<br /> <br /> <br /> Notice how the player must first lock-on to the guard and &quot;fires&quot; the bat swarm. Basically any time a player does this the targeted guard is imobilized and the player is able to sneak past. Basically it seems the guard plays an animation, he is unable to see the player, and a particle effect is &quot;connected&quot; to the guard in some way. I'm sure you know more about how that kind of system would be implemented the me though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well a locking system in a 3D world is not that easy. If you've played the Witcher series, you can see the evolution of the locking system through the years with, in witcher 3, a good locking system but it's still sometimes frustrating (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/witcher/comments/36uo0g/i_really_love_this_game_but_the_targeting_system/?st=ivxvgnys&amp;sh=ff629542\" target=\"_blank\">source</a>)<br /> The Assassin's creed series have a similar evolution but, the first witcher really had a very weird battle system whereas the Assassin's series was better from the beginning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007809#post1007809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that also apply to, say, the spell effects in Skyrim? There are quiet a few of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it does, of course, shaders are used for almost everything. Most shaders are simple enough, but some of them are very complex that's why in some video games you can see that the water is quite ugly and marvellous in others. Also, there's a huge difference between a static meteorological effect (some fog have been added by hand by a designer at the exact location) and a dynamical system (you turn in fog and can move around). With an imperfect fog effect and some work from the designer, you can obtain a magnificent scene, but you can't use this trick with dynamical fog.<br /> More generally, shaders are omnipresents in video game, the texture on a character is applied by a shader, the glass effect is a shader, same for metal and everything that you can classify as a material. Shaders are a big part of game development and, while mostly unknown, the major factor determining the visual quality of a game.<br /> I may be a bit too zealous, but if you want to learn more about it, <a href=\"http://thebookofshaders.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thebookofshaders.com/</a> is a good material.<br /> It's technical and you need to now programming, but there are many interactive examples that may help you to grasp the general idea of shaders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007809#post1007809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone is saying that a WoD game should be low-budget.<br /> <br /> If Paradox doesn't feel they have the resources to do the license proper justice they probably shouldn't have bought the rights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, having an enormous budget would be great, but investing a huge amount of money in a video game is a big risk for the company.<br /> The more budget you allow, the more the project will grow in size. Some companies can't handle project too ambitious, they simply don't have the manpower or the required experience to handle such large scale project.<br /> Also, doing &quot;proper justice&quot; to a license is subjective. You may imagine a 3D Adventure-RPG like Skyrim when someone else will imagine a 2D Baldur's like game.<br /> I don't have any details, but look at the previous MMO project of white wolf, nine years of development for nothing. CCP Games has surely lost quite an amount in this project, and they had experience with MMO (EVE online) so even with budget, time and experience it's not that easy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007809#post1007809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in regards to CD projekt using it's own technology, Unreal Engine recently became free, so any potential WoD developer could use that engine instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nothing is truly free<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Unreal Engine 4 is now available to everyone for free, and all future updates will be free!<br /> <br /> You can download the engine and use it for everything from game development, education, architecture, and visualization to VR, film and animation. When you ship a game or application, you pay a 5% royalty on gross revenue after the first $3,000 per product, per quarter. It\u2019s a simple arrangement in which we succeed only when you succeed. </div> </div> </div>5% on gross revenue is far from free, you can have a lot of gross revenue, but no profit at all. It's still a good option, but it's not free.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007826#post1007826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing a New World Order member could be the budget option. It would be hard to write the plot, dialogues and twists so that it simulates an NWO's mastery of Mind. But from what you said about technology costs, it is certainly cheaper to hire good writers and designers to write for an NWO game; compared to programming in different mystical powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I have absolutely no idea about what's the New World Order (sorry). But yes, I think that focusing on good narratives/atmosphere would have a better result than having every race, clan, tribes... developed.<br /> If I really insist on this point it's because I've seen too many projects being too ambitious from the start and finally ending with mediocre results.<br /> Creating a less ambitious game and expanding gradually the universe game after game is, in my opinion, the best solution to adapt WoD into video games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, please forgive my mistakes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12400-garyo","name":"GaryO","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12400_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T08:25:23-08:00","id":1008100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1007809#post1007809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Paradox doesn't feel they have the resources to do the license proper justice they probably shouldn't have bought the rights.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is my biggest worry of all.<br /> <br /> Although I heard they have all the assets and engine from CCPs game however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T11:59:43-08:00","id":1008230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008055#post1008055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I have absolutely no idea about what's the New World Order (sorry). But yes, I think that focusing on good narratives/atmosphere would have a better result than having every race, clan, tribes... developed.</div> </div> </div> </div>New World Order is one of the five Conventions of the Technocracy. Technocracy are a group of Mages (making up ~30+ % of them) who wield True Magick by treating the potential to change reality as strictly scientific - calling it Inspired Science. So instead of fireball spells they got plasma guns, instead of mystic flight they have anti-grav tech, instead of telepathy they have psychological analysis etc. New World Order is the Convention which specializes in Mind, and they do so through psychology, sociology, non-recreational drugs, subliminal broadcasts, etc. I consider the NWO to be the budget option because superb dialogue, player engagement &amp; choices, and plot would do be all you need to appropriately portray the breadth and potential of the NWO's Inspired Science.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008055#post1008055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I really insist on this point it's because I've seen too many projects being too ambitious from the start and finally ending with mediocre results..<br /> Creating a less ambitious game and expanding gradually the universe game after game is, in my opinion, the best solution to adapt WoD into video games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd call it focused, rather than less ambitious. But otherwise I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-26-2016, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T13:24:53-08:00","id":1008250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008055#post1008055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well a locking system in a 3D world is not that easy. If you've played the Witcher series, you can see the evolution of the locking system through the years with, in witcher 3, a good locking system but it's still sometimes frustrating (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/witcher/comments/36uo0g/i_really_love_this_game_but_the_targeting_system/?st=ivxvgnys&amp;sh=ff629542\" target=\"_blank\">source</a>)<br /> The Assassin's creed series have a similar evolution but, the first witcher really had a very weird battle system whereas the Assassin's series was better from the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... I never noticed any real problem with Witcher 3's targeting system, guess everyone's experience is different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008055#post1008055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, having an enormous budget would be great, but investing a huge amount of money in a video game is a big risk for the company.<br /> The more budget you allow, the more the project will grow in size. Some companies can't handle project too ambitious, they simply don't have the manpower or the required experience to handle such large scale project.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox has had a big commercial success with games like Cities Skylines, so I am going to give them the benefit of the doubt and assume that they feel they have the financial resources to take on this project.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008055#post1008055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, doing &quot;proper justice&quot; to a license is subjective. You may imagine a 3D Adventure-RPG like Skyrim when someone else will imagine a 2D Baldur's like game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it is, but I assume most fans, like myself, would prefer a successor to Bloodlines, which was similar to a Bethesda in a few ways, just without the open world. Basically what I'm hoping for is a game that is to VTM:B what Human Revolution was to Deus Ex, + as Veindark with modding tools, level editor, etc...<br /> <br /> I'm assuming Paradox knows this too, which gives me cause to hope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008055#post1008055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have any details, but look at the previous MMO project of white wolf, nine years of development for nothing. CCP Games has surely lost quite an amount in this project, and they had experience with MMO (EVE online) so even with budget, time and experience it's not that easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed that project went nowhere was because EVE Online was also being constantly worked on as well, with whole spin-off games being developed for it. I think having such a large project being continuously worked-on and maintained concurrently was soaking up their resources like a sponge. Why spend the money on one massive project when you have another already having proven an enormous success?<br /> <br /> Paradox shouldn't really have that problem because they would most likely farm the work out to another company (most likely Obsidian) who have a good track record of making acclaimed RPG's for other companies (Fallout: NV comes to mind) as well as making spiritual successors to older games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008055#post1008055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, nothing is truly free<br /> <br /> 5% on gross revenue is far from free, you can have a lot of gross revenue, but no profit at all. It's still a good option, but it's not free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but I'm sure it adds significantly less to development costs than having to pay +1000 or more per team member.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008055#post1008055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I have absolutely no idea about what's the New World Order (sorry). But yes, I think that focusing on good narratives/atmosphere would have a better result than having every race, clan, tribes... developed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree that it isn't really feasible to have a game where every supernatural race in the WoD is playable (though werewolf/fae/demon NPCs in a vampire game, for example, would be possible). But I do think you could get most of the clans playable in a game with a little tinkering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GaryO</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008055#post1008055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I really insist on this point it's because I've seen too many projects being too ambitious from the start and finally ending with mediocre results.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you're coming from here, but I'm going to trust that Paradox knew what they were doing when they purchased the rights, and that they know what they're doing with whatever game they're no-doubt working on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008100#post1008100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is my biggest worry of all.<br /> <br /> Although I heard they have all the assets and engine from CCPs game however.</div> </div> </div> </div>They would most likely have Obsidian develop the project, which could mean we get something like New Vegas, or PoE with Vampires.<br /> <br /> They also did an RPG survey a while back which asked about games like Mass Effect and Bloodlines, they also asked about mod support, so that's a good sign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T15:16:54-08:00","id":1008288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008250#post1008250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would most likely have Obsidian develop the project, which could mean we get something like New Vegas, or PoE with Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter is also one of my biggest worries since I really hope they actually don't turn WoD/Vampire into a Isomatric game like PoE and Tyranny. I just hope they use CCP's engine and assets and put them into good use to go with the route of New Vegas as in being a AAA third/first person Action-RPG game.<br /> <br /> It would be quite funny to use CCP's engine and assets to turn something that was once was going to be a MMO is now a single player campaign with heavy modding support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-25-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T15:35:44-08:00","id":1008296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008288#post1008288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The latter is also one of my biggest worries since I really hope they actually don't turn WoD/Vampire into a Isomatric game like PoE and Tyranny. I just hope they use CCP's engine and assets and put them into good use to go with the route of New Vegas as in being a AAA third/first person Action-RPG game.<br /> <br /> It would be quite funny to use CCP's engine and assets to turn something that was once was going to be a MMO is now a single player campaign with heavy modding support.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the same way, but I saw some screenshots of the unfinished game, the graphics looked kinda... MMO-ish, not exactly what people might expect from a modern AAA Action-RPG. Might be better if they used the concept art (which looked badass) and move development to an engine like Unreal.<br /> <br /> I would be slightly surprised, and disappointed, if they made a WoD game into an isometric nostalgia trip, since it wouldn't have much nostalgic value. The developers know that anything they create will be compared to Bloodlines, and I really don't see how they could decide that such a radical departure in terms of style would be the way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T16:07:38-08:00","id":1008311,"title":"","content":"Going through the Lores of Demons, well, a lot of them would be a bit iffy. The two common Lores could work fine enough, Flame would just be a base damage power, Awakening for healing, Winds for when you need to Darth Vader someone, Paths and Portals if you want to teleport, Light to create distractions, Longing for talking to people, Storms for water powers, Transfiguration for disguises, Beast for animal powers, Flesh for temporary boosts and healing... and that's about it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Slayers would have enough to be a game on their own: Death for combat purposes, Realms for teleporting between the mortal and spirit worlds and Spirit for dealing with spirits. That could work, but it wouldn't be much of a WoD game if it was just them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1005273#post1005273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines came out in 2003 or 2004 didn't it? Games are enormously more complex these days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Complexer to make, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T16:14:54-08:00","id":1008313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008311#post1008311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Complexer to make, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, because the game they're making is much more complex. Not just visually, but in the AI and abilities that player characters can perform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:33:20-08:00","id":1008360,"title":"","content":"World of Darkness MMO<br /> So here is my answer to WOD MMO. Yes it can be done and done well but not the traditional way of MMO\u2019s.<br /> First you must build a world which is total interactive. Many games out there have done this such has Skyrm and Red Faction. This would create a world which you can kick down any door and level any building. But with that comes the great part to a WOD MMO. Unlike all other MMO\u2019s your actions are what generate quest/missions for other players. A vampire who feeds in a sloppy manor finds themselves in trouble in different ways. To start if an NPC watches it could report it to the local NPC law enforcement or spread a video on the WOD Web. This would alert Elder NPC\u2019s to send someone out to bring in the character to have a discussion about their actions or maybe a Hunter gets an information he can use to move in on a Haven or even get his first sets of fangs. Player triggered missions would then start the ball rolling but it does not end there. Now you have those people who run amuck and act crazy well then you would have a system like in APB reloaded which would up the threat level and response to the point that the mad insane werewolf who is dry thumping the people in the park after killing them because he thinks it\u2019s funny. Now he is the prey of something much stronger than him and its coming for him in the park and now he is on the run or dead. But wait can\u2019t he just make another character and repeat this action. Sure he can but there a cool down of threat level, he will now have to lay low or quickly gain more threat which could repeat the same actions or attract player attention which would be also bad. Now outside of player actions you would have ST\u2019s going around playing NPC characters who would be working towards a goal or taking over an area for their supernatural group or trying to take a group of players or NPC out of an area. Every time you succeed at a goal be it physical mental or social it would gain point which you could use to increase your character ability. Cities would be almost equal size to their counter parts to allow more room to grow power, and this would help bring new content to future book coming out. Picture you\u2019re a lone Bone Gnawer working the docks and group of BSD players are guarding a shipment which is being put on a boat. Players would have to maintain control of the area until the shipment has left but you cannot turn the tides and let your Pack (guild) or Sept (whole city) know by making a single howl which those who are not garou would not understand. The WOD MMO would be a game of resources and reactions. This is your neighborhood are you going to let Pentext buy out all the businesses or the Technocracy invade the mortals fate, or will you let your neighbors be food for the Sabbat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T04:32:29-08:00","id":1008487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004586-how-would-a-wod-computer-video-game-would-work?p=1008313#post1008313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yes, because the game they're making is much more complex. Not just visually, but in the AI and abilities that player characters can perform.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be nice to actually see some of that complexity again for a change. And complex AI and actions for the player are not complex gameplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}